The content focused on expanding my knowledge of Linux, exploring more advanced command-line operations and understanding how the system manages files, directories,
and user access.
I practiced using command arguments and flags to improve command execution and gain more control over terminal operations. I also worked with file management,
learning how to copy and move files, as well as exploring important directories within the Linux filesystem.

Another important topic was remote access through SSH, which allowed me to understand how to connect to Linux machines remotely and interact with them through the terminal.
Additionally, I learned about Linux permissions, users, and groups, understanding how access to files and directories is controlled
and how to identify the permissions assigned to different users.

The practical exercises helped me strengthen my command-line skills, understand system access management,
and become more confident when working independently in Linux environments.
These concepts are essential for system administration and provide an important foundation for further development in Cybersecurity.
